<p>pylock.toml is the standard version of the same idea: a TOML file that records, for every package, the version, where the file came from, and its hash. nab writes it with nab lock, and pip 26.1 can install it, though that support is still experimental. uv projects also keep uv.lock, uv's own lock file.</p>
